[[Zhalia Moon]] came into possession of a Kilthane Amulet during her teenage years while working for [[the Organization]]. {{Source|S1E11}} 

During the fight for the Amulet of [[Metagolem]] in the [[Golem's Attic]], Zhalia invoked her Kilthane Titan. He was attacked by some [[Suits]]. After the defeat of [[Caliban]], Kilthane attacked Grier's [[Breaker]] but was overpowered and defeated. {{Source|Words of Truth, Heart of Lies}} 

Kilthane was later invoked to fight the [[Organization]] in the [[Cave of the Gargoyle]]. Kilthane fought some [[Redcap]] Titans and Breaker but was defeated. {{Source|Into the River of Secrets}} In the [[Paris Catacombs]], Kilthane fought against the [[Knights of Arc's Inner Circle]] but was defeated. {{Source|Crawling the Catacombs}} Zhalia invoked Kilthane to fight [[DeFoe]]'s forces. Kilthane shielded Zhalia from DeFoe's attacks and defeated some Redcap Titans but was injured by [[Kreutalk]]'s Acid Attack ability. When [[Dante]] arrived, Kilthane recovered and, along with Caliban, advanced on DeFoe and his Suits, forcing them to retreat. {{Source|Divide and Conquer}}

Zhalia summoned Kilthane in [[Iceland]] to fight against [[Ymir]]'s army of [[Ice Creatures]]. {{Source|The Legacy of Thor}} Zhalia later invoked Kilthane in the [[Temple of Thor]] to protect Dante from the wild Titan, [[Fenris]]. Although Kilthane delivered a powerful strike on Fenris, he was defeated due to the temple's effect on Fenris' strength. {{Source|Two Powers Become One}}

Kilthane was invoked in the [[Basilisk House]] a surprise attack on DeFoe and his men. Kilthane charged at [[Mindrone]] before being bear-hugged by Breaker. He was freed when [[Sophie]]'s [[Sabriel]] hit Breaker and retreated with Zhalia, Sophie and Sabriel, closely followed by Grier, a Suit, Breaker and Mindrone. {{Source|Absent Heroes}}

Kilthane was mentioned by [[Cherit]] to be heavy enough to walk underwater. Zhalia invoked Kilthane to cover the team after a surprise attack made by DeFoe's forces. {{Source|The Treasures of the Argonauts}} On [[Madea Island]], an illusion of Kilthane was invoked by an illusion of Zhalia to attack the real Zhalia. However, the illusional Kilthane was defeated by Caliban. {{Source|The Beautiful Trap}}

In [[Newgrange Passage Tomb]], Kilthane fought and defeated a [[Bonelasher]] in a fight with [[Klaus]]' Suits. {{Source|Home Turf}} Zhalia later summoned Kilthane to fight against a Bonelasher and [[Enforcer]] in Klaus' lab, in order to maintain her cover as a double agent. {{Source|The Bookshop Hunter}} In the [[Castle of Vlad Dracul]], Kilthane fought against [[Sabriel]], [[Feyone]] and [[Icarus]] in the [[Castle of Vlad Dracul]]. {{Source|The Vampire Loses Its Fangs}}

At the [[Temple of Poseidon]], Kilthane fought against [[Rassimov]]'s [[Anubian]] but was defeated. {{Source|The Unseen Guide}} Kilthane attacked and defeated an [[Enforcer]] in [[Ethiopia]]. {{Source|The Golden Asp}} Later, in [[King Solomon's Mines]], Kilthane fought with [[the Professor]]'s [[Dominator]], only to be defeated by [[Rassimov]]'s [[Hopeshatter]] power. {{Source|To Be Together}}

On the roof of [[Dante's house]], Zhalia invoked Kilthane against the Professor. However, [[Araknos]]'s Mastermind ability took control of Kilthane leading to him fighting with Sabriel and [[Lindorm]] before being defeated by Caliban. {{Source|The Secret of Two Generations}} At [[the Professor's castle]] Kilthane fought alongside [[Lok]]'s [[Freelancer]] against [[Jokoul]] and [[Strix]]. Kilthane then stabbed and defeated [[Terrapede]]. {{Source|The Divine Comedy}}

On a mission to the English coast, Kilthane was invoked to defend the Huntik team from the Casterwill guardians, [[Mallory]] and [[White]]. Kilthane then defeated White's [[Feyone]]. {{Source|Cave of the Casterwills}} Kilthane was later summoned in the [[Casterwill Library]] and concealed by Zhalia's [[Thoughtspecter]] power. He later overpowered [[Lane]] in order to stop [[Lucas Casterwill]]'s team. {{Source|Chasing Void}}

On the longest night of the year, Zhalia invoked Kilthane during a cave-in to help her carry [[Den]] and [[Harrison Fears]] to safety. When Zhalia went to fight [[the Betrayer]], Kilthane was ordered to guard the two brothers but was sacrificed by Harrison's [[Powermark]] spell to give both Harrison and Den energy to battle the Betrayer. {{Source|Lok and the Betrayer}}

